[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isic-5820 persistent systemd deployment on gad"], :adr/topic "isic-5820-persistent-deployment", :adr/related ["adr-2607173300" "adr-2607173400" "adr-2607173100"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607173500-isic-5820-persistent-deployment", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-18", :adr/body "# ADR-2607173500: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 -- persistent production deployment (systemd, tailnet-reachable)\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-18\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive: \\\"\u6280\u8853\u7a74\u57cb\u3081\\\" -- second half, following ADR-2607173400's Lead/Contact entities)\n**Scope**: fleet node `gad` (murakumo fleet), new systemd service. No superproject/child-repo code changes.\n\n## Context\n\nThe coverage assessment (ADR-2607173300) found: \\\"No live deployed CRM product instance -- the 'live now' claim in business-model.md is a Stripe *billing* checkout link, not a running product URL.\\\" This ADR closes that gap: `crm.http` (the actor's existing, previously-never-deployed HTTP service layer) now runs continuously.\n\n## Decision\n\n**Host**: `gad` (murakumo fleet node, already running `llama-server` for fleet-main / ADR-2607173100) -- chosen because it already has JDK 21 + Clojure CLI + git, is already the fleet's established systemd-service host, and colocating with the model server lets the CRM's real-model advisor call `localhost:11434` directly (no network hop, no public-endpoint dependency).\n\n- **Checkout**: `/home/gad/services/isic-5820/orgs/{cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5820, kotoba-lang/{crm,langgraph,langchain}}` -- same sibling `:local/root` layout as the superproject's `orgs/` tree, cloned read-only from each repo's GitHub `main`.\n- **Service**: systemd unit `isic5820-crm.service`, `User=gad`, `ExecStart=clojure -M:serve` (the actor's own `deps.edn` `:serve` alias, unmodified), `Restart=on-failure`.\n- **Config** (`/etc/isic5820/env`, mode 600, root:root): `ISIC5820_API_TOKEN` (freshly generated random secret, stored in kagi vault `gftdcojp/ISIC5820_API_TOKEN` -- never in a commit, never echoed in any log this session), `ISIC5820_HTTP_PORT=8092`, `ISIC5820_STORE_FILE=/var/lib/isic5820/db.edn` (durable `crm.file-store/FileStore`, per the actor's own existing durability design -- NOT the ephemeral in-memory default), `ISIC5820_MODEL_PROVIDER=openai` + `ISIC5820_MODEL_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions` + `ISIC5820_MODEL=fleet-main` -- points at whatever model the `llama-server.service` unit is currently serving (qwen3.6-35b-a3b as of ADR-2607173100); switching the fleet's main model (editing that unit's `ExecStart`) is picked up by this CRM service automatically on its next restart, no isic-5820-side change needed, consistent with the repo-wide murakumo-main switchability principle.\n- **Store seed**: `/var/lib/isic5820/db.edn` initialized to a **genuinely empty** dataset (`{:reps {} :accounts {} :opportunities {} :subscriptions {} :leads {} :contacts {} :ledger []}`) -- deliberately NOT `crm.store/demo-data` (fictitious Acme Corp etc.). This is cloud-itonami's real, currently-empty sales pipeline, not a demo. Zero fabricated business data.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `systemctl is-active` = active; `/health` = `{\\\"status\\\":\\\"ok\\\",\\\"store\\\":\\\"reachable\\\"}`.\n- Startup log confirms real-model wiring: `RevOps-LLM advisor = REAL MODEL (provider=openai model=fleet-main url=http://localhost:11434/v1/chat/completions)` -- NOT the sealed mock.\n- `POST /propose` exercised twice over the tailnet (bearer-token-authenticated): phase 0 correctly HOLDs (`:phase-disabled`, read-only phase); phase 3 against a lead-id that legitimately does not exist in this empty store correctly triggers a governed HOLD path -- the real model detected the missing entity and drafted a (structurally valid but imperfectly-worded) proposal, the governor's mechanics processed it without crashing or fabricating data.\n- **Real-model observation worth recording**: on that missing-entity case, the live model chose `:effect :correction-apply` (a kind meant for `:dispute/request` patches) instead of a cleaner \\\"not found\\\" shape, and `crm.store`'s `:correction-apply` commit path is hardcoded to write into `:opportunities` regardless of the actual op -- this produced one harmless `{\\\"lead-100\\\" nil}` garbage key. Not a security or data-integrity issue (no real entity was touched), but a genuine gap: `:correction-apply`'s effect handler doesn't validate `:patch` is present or that the target entity type matches the op. Reset the store to the clean empty seed rather than leaving test pollution; **left the underlying gap as a flagged follow-up, not fixed here** (scope: today's directive was entity coverage + deployment, not hardening every effect handler against an adversarial/confused model).\n- **Public (non-tailnet) exposure was NOT completed**: 1Password CLI session expired mid-task (`account is not signed in`) blocking the Cloudflare API DNS step; re-authenticating a credential session is explicitly the owner's action, not something this agent performs. The service is reachable now over the tailnet (`http://<gad-tailnet-ip>:8092`) to anyone with tailnet access, which already includes the owner. Public hostname (`crm-5820.gftd.ai`, mirroring `qwen-gad.gftd.ai`'s pattern) is a same-day follow-up once 1Password is re-authenticated.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- cloud-itonami now has a real, continuously-running, governed CRM instance an operator can actually use -- not just a library invoked from a REPL/test.\n- Follow-ups: public hostname (pending 1Password re-auth), an approval-submission endpoint for escalated ops (already a documented gap in `docs/api.md`, unrelated to this deployment), hardening `:correction-apply`'s effect handler against a mismatched op/entity type.\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-18", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607173500: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 persistent production deployment (systemd, gad, tailnet-reachable)", :adr/source-format "edn"}]